                <pb facs="0766" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg668"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.711/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-22T19:00:00+08:00">December 22, 1932—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 22—6:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1376. Shanghai’s December 21, noon, regarding <hi rendition="#italic">Far Eastern
                        Review</hi>. I assume that action by Chinese Government was taken for the
                    purpose of punishing its owner and editor who has gone to Geneva as an adviser
                    to the government of Manchukuo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
